# Commit Intent Routing

When the user expresses commit intent in natural language, always run the full
`git-commit` skill workflow (`.cursor/skills/git-commit/SKILL.md`).

The `git-commit` skill is the single canonical commit path — it covers
untracked-file confirmation, security scanning, test verification, and atomic
commit guidance. Do not fall back to a shortened `git commit` that skips those
safety steps.

## Trigger Phrases

Treat any of these as a commit intent:

- `commit`
- `commit this`
- `commit and push`
- `push this` / `push to remote`
- `save changes` / `save this`
- `finalize changes`

## Required Behavior

- Run the `git-commit` skill end-to-end. Do not use a shortened `git commit`
  path that skips the skill's safety steps.
- Keep all safeguards (untracked-file confirm, secret scan, test run, atomic
  commit, no tool-attribution footer).

## Example

- User: `commit and push`
- Assistant: execute the `git-commit` skill workflow (Steps 0–8) before any
  commit/push.
